WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:07.037
"Edible Skin Care—Sun Protection
from the Inside Out"

00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.960
A Nature article
"Edible skin care"

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.480
underscored an opportunity

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:14.560
provided by
the skin's rapid turnover.

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:17.200
Our entire outer layer of skin

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:19.720
is completely regrown
every month

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:21.240
from the nutrients
we provide it,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:24.400
so we are what we eat
not just years down the road,

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.640
but on a month-to-month basis.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.000
For example, the amount
of vitamin C we eat

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.200
maps directly
onto the amount of vitamin C

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:32.960
we have in our skin.

00:00:32.960 --> 00:00:35.200
Take skin frailty.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:38.440
Skin atrophy with age
is not just a cosmetic issue.

00:00:38.440 --> 00:00:41.320
It can result in skin tears,
bruising, itching.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:43.280
A cross-sectional study
of dietary intake

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:46.000
and skin frailty
found that dietary patterns

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:48.880
characterized by higher
vegetable and fruit intake

00:00:48.880 --> 00:00:51.360
were associated
with better skin condition.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.640
To test the effects of greens,

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.520
Korean researchers
randomized women

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.800
to one of two doses
of chlorophyl

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.560
(equivalent to up
to a few tablespoons (29.60 ml)

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:01.520
of cooked spinach a day).

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:02.560
After three months,

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.920
skin biopsies showed
a significant increase

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.480
in collagen production,

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.160
accompanied by an increase
in skin elasticity

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:11.800
and a decrease
in facial wrinkles.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.080
This may have been due in part

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.640
to an "inside-out"
sunscreen effect,

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:17.760
as less DNA damage was noted

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:21.040
after the same degree
of UV radiation.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:23.800
Unfortunately, these were all
just comparisons to baseline,

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.800
as there was no control arm
included.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.520
Still, this is the kind
of evidence cited

00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:30.440
by dermatology journal
commentaries

00:01:30.440 --> 00:01:33.360
with titles like "Eat Plenty
of Green Leafy Vegetables

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:35.200
for Photoprotection."

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.480
(Protection against the sun.)

00:01:37.480 --> 00:01:38.600
There have been

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.280
placebo-controlled
randomized trials.

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.520
Compared to placebo,

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.520
ten months (but not five)
of an extract of curly kale

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.240
caused a significant improvement

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:51.760
in a noninvasive measure
of skin collagen status.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.080
The researchers concluded
"a healthy lifestyle

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:55.920
including a diet
rich in carotenoids

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.640
is the best prevention strategy

00:01:57.640 --> 00:01:59.840
against premature skin aging."

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.120
Randomized, double-blind,

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.560
placebo-controlled
clinical trials

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:06.520
also found apple extracts
can protect the skin

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:08.840
against the sun after 12 weeks,

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.080
as can a combination

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.160
of rosemary
and grapefruit extracts

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:13.560
after just 2 weeks,

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:16.880
though a blackcurrant
juice drink for 6 weeks

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:21.000
or a pomegranate extract
for 4 weeks did not.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.160
What about whole foods?

00:02:23.160 --> 00:02:25.720
Researchers burned
the butts of twenty women

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:26.960
with a UV lamp

00:02:26.960 --> 00:02:28.720
before and after
half of them ate

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:30.800
three tablespoons (44.40 ml)
of tomato paste a day

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:32.280
for three months.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:35.800
There was significantly less
DNA damage in the derrieres

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.400
of those who had been eating
the tomatoes,

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.040
as well as a reduction
in the collagen-eating enzyme

00:02:41.040 --> 00:02:42.680
that plays a role in skin aging

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.240
activated by UV-induced
oxidative stress.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.920
In mice, eating tomatoes
translates

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:51.480
into fewer UV-induced
skin cancers,

00:02:51.480 --> 00:02:56.160
but no such long-term studies
have been performed in people.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.440
DNA is damaged directly
by UV-B rays,

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:02.200
whereas the bulk
of UV radiation from the sun-

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:06.280
UV-A rays-damages DNA indirectly

00:03:06.280 --> 00:03:07.840
by producing free radicals

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:11.720
that deplete the antioxidant
levels in our skin.

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.880
Dietary tomato paste protects

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:16.840
against UV-induced skin redness
in humans.

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.240
If we eat a lot
of anti-oxidant rich food,

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:20.240
such as tomato paste,

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:24.160
even just ten weeks before
swimsuit season (but not four),

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.600
we can reduce the redness
of a sunburn by 40 percent.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.320
Eating grapes may also cut down
on UV-induced DNA damage

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:33.320
and inflammation.

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:37.320
It's like we have
built-in sunscreen in our skin.

00:03:37.320 --> 00:03:40.020
Now, this isn't as good
as a high SPF sunblock,

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.000
and we shouldn't be sunbathing
in the first place,

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:45.920
but damage occurs every time
we are exposed to the sun

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:47.600
and much of that exposure
occurs

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:51.320
when our skin is
otherwise unprotected.

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.800
Just giving people supplements
containing the same amount

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:55.240
of the red pigment lycopene

00:03:55.240 --> 00:03:57.840
failed to have
a significant effect,

00:03:57.840 --> 00:03:59.880
suggesting it's
the constellation

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.520
of antioxidant constituents
in whole tomatoes

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:04.760
working together.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:07.640
An excellent example
of this nutrient synergy

00:04:07.640 --> 00:04:10.040
is the fact that even
mega-doses of vitamin C

00:04:10.040 --> 00:04:13.200
or vitamin E alone
have no significant effect

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:16.520
on photoprotection
(skin defense against UV rays),

00:04:16.520 --> 00:04:18.920
but when combined,

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:21.160
they increase
the UV radiation dose needed

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:25.400
to cause the same redness
by more than 75 percent.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:27.560
See, antioxidants
often work together.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:30.920
Vitamin C, for example,
regenerates vitamin E

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.840
once it becomes oxidized itself.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:37.360
However, some carotenoids
can stand on their own.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:38.560
Giving people the equivalent

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:41.320
of one to two daily servings
of dark green leafies' worth

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:44.280
of lutein and zeaxanthin
significantly improves

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.600
skin hydration, elasticity,
and photoprotection

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.920
starting within just two weeks.

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:51.840
Beta carotene works too.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:54.600
A meta-analysis of seven
randomized controlled trials

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:56.800
found that a daily dose
as low as a cup (240 g)

00:04:56.800 --> 00:04:58.400
of sweet potatoes' worth

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.520
protects your skin
from sunburn,

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.760
but it takes
a minimum of 10 weeks

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.800
to sufficiently build up
in your skin.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.720
Skin biopsies also show
that diet-relevant doses

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.320
of beta-carotene can boost
collagen production four-fold

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.880
and decrease UV-induced
DNA damage by 30 percent,

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:19.280
combined with an improvement
in facial wrinkles

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:22.680
and skin elasticity
over a period of three months.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.760
There was no control group,
though,

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:26.720
and a much larger, longer study

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:29.080
found that the same dose
of beta-carotene failed

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:31.440
to affect skin aging
over four years' time

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.640
compared to placebo.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:36.280
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:05:36.280 --> 00:05:38.640
of coenzyme Q10

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:41.760
found it didn't provide
any UV protection,

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:43.880
but it was able to reduce
crow's feet wrinkles

00:05:43.880 --> 00:05:47.600
by about 10 percent compared
to placebo within 12 weeks,

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.400
with no significant difference
reported

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:52.320
between groups getting
a low dose (50 milligrams a day)

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.400
or a high one
(150 milligrams a day).

00:05:56.400 --> 00:05:59.040
Topical sunscreens
and dietary photoprotection

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:01.480
from foods like greens
and sweet potatoes

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:03.720
represent
complementary strategies

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:05.800
for safeguarding our skin.

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.040
Sunscreens have the advantage
of working almost immediately

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.960
and offering
much stronger shielding.

00:06:11.960 --> 00:06:14.640
Produce protection builds up
slowly over weeks

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:18.640
and only achieves an SPF of 4,
compared to 10 to 40

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.040
or even higher sun protection

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:22.600
factor within
typical sunscreens.

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:24.080
On the other hand,

00:06:24.080 --> 00:06:26.720
sunscreens have to be
deliberately applied

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.920
in sufficient amounts
and with sufficient coverage

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:31.360
(including
all the hard-to-reach places),

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:33.640
and then still can rub
or sweat off,

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:36.720
whereas the protection
from plants is ever-present

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:38.840
and built-in all over.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:57.520
Combined, they naturally
complement each other.

